Package: InterconectaR
Version: 1.0.1
Date: 2026-09-23
Title: Tools for Network Analysis and Psychometric Insights
Encoding: UTF-8
Authors@R: person("José", "Ventura-León",
                  email = "jventuraleon@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2996-4244"))
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Description: Provides tools for psychological network analysis and
    psychometric modeling in the social sciences. It estimates networks by
    group, summarises centrality and bridge centrality indices, evaluates
    the stability of edges and centrality from bootstrap results, refines
    items by the stability of exploratory graph analysis (EGA), and plots
    networks with the variance explained of each node. It also estimates
    an a priori sample size for EGA through Monte Carlo simulation and
    includes an interactive application to plan the sample size of a
    network study. Methods follow Epskamp, Borsboom
    and Fried (2018) <doi:10.3758/s13428-017-0862-1> and Golino and
    Epskamp (2017) <doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0174035>.
